Third-party content and provenance
=================================

The tractoverse brand artifacts (logos, theme, colors) embed / derive from the
following third-party works. This NOTICE records provenance and license for
every vendored or bundled component, in line with the package licensing rule
(verify that each redistributed library permits the exact use).

1. Font Awesome (icon glyphs embedded in the package logos)
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   The per-package emblems (fiber: bezier-curve, master: blender, rtists:
   palette, riot: feather-pointed, toad: book-atlas, bot:
   magnifying-glass-chart) are Font Awesome Free icons.
   - Source: Font Awesome Free (https://fontawesome.com),
     FortAwesome/Font-Awesome (github.com/FortAwesome/Font-Awesome), Free 6.5.2.
   - Delivered in R through the 'fontawesome' R package v0.5.3
     (github.com/rstudio/fontawesome; CRAN).
   - License (per the bundled all.css header):
       Icons:  CC BY 4.0 (Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International)
       Fonts:  SIL OFL 1.1
       Code:   MIT License
     License reference: https://fontawesome.com/license/free
     SPDX: CC-BY-4.0 (icons).
   - Use: The SVG glyphs are rasterized (via rsvg) into the package logos
     distributed as PNG in `inst/brand/logos/`. This is permitted under
     CC BY 4.0 and Font Awesome's free-license terms WITH ATTRIBUTION.
   - Attribution: "Font Awesome Free 6.5.2 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com
     (Icons: CC BY 4.0, Fonts: SIL OFL 1.1, Code: MIT License)". Copyright
     2024 Fonticons, Inc.

2. three.js (used by the tractoverse render pipeline, NOT bundled here)
   --------------------------------------------------------------------
   The logo glyphs are rendered with the rtists R package, which vendors
   three.js r186 (MIT). tractoverse itself does NOT redistribute the three.js
   bundle; it only ships the resulting PNG renders. See rtists/inst/NOTICE for
   the three.js MIT provenance and NOTICE (Copyright (c) 2010-2026 Three.js
   Authors, SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT).

3. htmlwidgets.js / htmltools CSS in the served preview (NOT bundled here)
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------
   Local preview outputs under the build scratch directory (`serve/`) embed
   htmlwidgets (MIT) and htmltools fill.css. These are development-only render
   previews and are not shipped with tractoverse.

4. pkgdown favicons (derived from the in-house tractoverse logo)
   -------------------------------------------------------------
   `pkgdown/favicon/*` are favicon sizes rasterized from the in-house
   tractoverse logo by the RealFaviconGenerator service
   (https://realfavicongenerator.net). The output is the user's own artwork at
   various resolutions, so no third-party copyrightable content is introduced;
   the service applies no license to the generated images. The SVG carries its
   metadata attribution (`dc:creator` / `dc:source`) in-file.

Provenance of the tractoverse brand palette
-------------------------------------------
The brand palette (GitHub-dark shell #0d1117 + per-package vibrant hues) is
drawn from the tractoverse useR! 2026 talk by Aymeric Stamm
(https://astamm.github.io/talks/2026-07-09-tractoverse/), specifically its
index.qmd + custom.css.
